# Configured operation

Read docs/MISSION_CONTROL_LOCAL_API.md. Provision installation identity, migrations,
restricted roles and accepted runtime options before startup; startup is read-only.

```powershell
uv sync
docker compose up -d
uv run python -m mission_control.bootstrap.preflight
uv run uvicorn mission_control.bootstrap.api:create_app --factory --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000
uv run python -m mission_control.bootstrap.worker
```

The worker requires explicit selected application and binding pin. CLI missionctl
uses the signed application-scoped API. Agent Server's canonical configuration is
agent_server/langgraph.json and never defines a competing mission scheduler.

Readiness is production_common only (common release installed by mission-db);
local disposable proof is not a live installation.
Never point application services at Temporal's private database. Never remove
Compose volumes or user records to fix readiness. No live destructive changes or
paid provider qualification without authorization.
